{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556897-using-ai-to-do-a-solo-chronicle","id":1556897,"title":"Using AI to do a solo chronicle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-22T06:39:17-08:00","id":1556897,"title":"Using AI to do a solo chronicle?","content":"Has anyone tried to use AI to do a solo chronicle i.e. the AI is the storyteller and you are the PC? I'm 14 sessions in and it is real hit-or-miss. Biggest problems are<br /> 1. AI forgets or makes up it's own rules (admittedly Mage is a complicated game)<br /> 2. Forgets key Chronicle story points or character details<br /> 3. Struggles to introduce meaningful conflict into story<br /> <br /> Despite this, sometimes it hits a groove and it is kind of fun (or at least more fun than playing a video game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T06:53:47-08:00","id":1556899,"title":"","content":"I have thought of it before although not for Mage specifically. My biggest reason for not doing it so far is your note #3. On the other hand I'm not convinced I can introduce meaningful conflict into a story at times!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T07:54:25-08:00","id":1556901,"title":"","content":"Well, its not so much that it (Claude) can't think of good plot hooks. Its that its NPC interactions are kind of weak. I just did a scene where my character was at a club and a Seer who has been hunting for me walked in. And I was like &quot;Oh no. This is about to get real&quot; and so the Seer was like &quot;Hey I've been looking for you&quot;. And my character was like &quot;I don't know who you are and you're bothering me&quot; (manipulation + subterfuge, four successes) and the Seer was like &quot;Oh. Ok. Sorry&quot; and left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T10:21:41-08:00","id":1556913,"title":"","content":"I think it'll get better when people start seeing the money in making gamemaster AIs but I don't think they're ready for it. I've heard of people doing this aside from you (like with Madmarcus, not with mage, but with other storytelling games). Recounting it always seems disjointed like they're playing with someone who doesn't know storytelling or the game specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T10:34:32-08:00","id":1556914,"title":"","content":"Like I said, MtAW is a very complex game with a lot of moving parts (both fluff and crunch). I'm sure it would have no trouble running a simple dungeon crawl or monster encounter. The overall story makes sense (maybe I'll do an actual play thread). It's more that individual NPC encounters are sometimes like &quot;Wait, what?&quot;<br /> <br /> It also depends on the player probably. I'm a very proactive player, and I prefer a more sandbox-y style of play, so I'm doing a lot of the steering of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T13:37:43-08:00","id":1556924,"title":"","content":"It's not the complexity of the rules (that's actually simple for computation) that's the issue.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it's not money either. The current generation of models do not have the internal algorithmic functions to replace a ST(/DM/etc.):<br /> <br /> 1) They lack a capacity for a &quot;world state&quot; memory. Without that they can't remember character details, know how to assign attachment values of specific rules to specific situations, and have the foundation for approximating point 2.<br /> <br /> 2) They do not have a computational method to understand &quot;meaningful&quot; conflict. The models do not understand meaning at all. They assign values based on inputs of how often certain strings get connected to other strings, and use that probability to simulate. Without being able to even examine what's in the strings, they can't even &quot;perceive&quot; what the contents mean to us. So higher order operations like &quot;meaningful conflict&quot; is simply out of reach.<br /> <br /> 3) This is also why they have no ability to recognize when they output something incorrectly, or have made up a fabricated response instead of a true response (even if you are using a small dataset). We can recognize if we are struggle to come up with a creative idea, we can know we've forgotten something, and so on. These models are not capable of that because it's outside their programming to consider such things. &quot;Hallucinations&quot; by these systems are inherent to how they work. Probabilistic systems are supposed to generate outlier outputs over time, so they're always going to have a chance of a dramatic failure and insert something unhelpful if used for extended periods on the same task.<br /> <br /> There are ways you can do more work to help out (such as generating/updating a world state document and instructing it be referenced in your prompts to act as &quot;memory&quot;), but that somewhat defeats the exercise over using traditional solo TTRPG systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T14:19:35-08:00","id":1556925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556897-using-ai-to-do-a-solo-chronicle?p=1556913#post1556913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'll get better when people start seeing the money in making gamemaster AIs but I don't think they're ready for it. I've heard of people doing this aside from you (like with Madmarcus, not with mage, but with other storytelling games). Recounting it always seems disjointed like they're playing with someone who doesn't know storytelling or the game specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no money in gamemaster AIs.<br /> <br /> This is partially because tabletop game RP is a niche interest, but primarily because there's no money in the large language models we're talking about in the first place. The models currently being developed require hundreds of millions of dollars on datacenters. OpenAI operates at a loss, and this loss is in operating costs, meaning getting more customers would mean they would run a <i>bigger</i> loss. No progress has really been shown on addressing the fundamental problem of hallucination, which appears to be a structural issue with the technology and how it works.<br /> <br /> The models' tendency towards well-trod clich\u00e9s you could have thought of yourself are also a structural result of how the models work. They're very complicated rearrangements of words based on statistical relationships in proximity to other words in a vast set of training data. The same reason that the phrases it spits out are impressive reproductions of real speech, right down to fluent use of slang and abbreviation, is the reason why it's going to tend towards the most common stock answer in any situation: it defaults to the average.<br /> <br /> Debates about the technology aside, it's a bad fit for creative writing, because the strength of the technology is in its ability to <i>not</i> heavily deviate or innovate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T00:44:49-08:00","id":1556954,"title":"","content":"I've been working a lot with DeepSeek lately, and while I will point some disagreements with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Stupid Loserman</a> here, the bulk of it is spot on. They may seem to have a lot of capacity for this task (and they do have a lot for a lot of tasks), but this simply isn't true. And a lot of the problem boils down to something that plagued AIs and AI predictions since the beginning: what seems to be the easy part for us isn't easy at all, it's just our brains being very good at those tasks.<br /> <br /> One of the key problems is still the size of the Context Window, roughly speaking how much data they can work with at a given time. They're getting pretty decent for some things, but a TTRPG involves a helluva lot of individual tokens. Even if you manage to build a World State memory it will occupy a lot of context and severely limit what you can do from then on. And the longer the story goes, the worse it gets.<br /> <br /> &quot;Meaningful&quot; is another thing that you can try to simulate through an algorithm, but on top of being hard it'll eat up your context window, and the result isn't guaranteed. And as said, money simply isn't the solution, the fundamental problem is a mix of serious technological constraints and a huge processing cost that keeps it way beyond anything resembling profit. LLMs are strategic tech and research objects, they're mostly operating at loss and offering services just because our use of them generates valuable data for their development.<br /> <br /> Well. There's a few exceptions, but nothing to write home about. Even then, you can always try Character Ai or similar options. They're weak and limited, but trained to cover storytelling techniques (for a given value of it, anyway). Or you can get an API (if you have the money) or a free model like DeepSeek and run locally, but then you'll be on yourself to do the training and the result will still have a series of limitations, even more than running from the cloud (obviously).<br /> <br /> Now, the few things I disagree with them: first, the main problems can be at least partially solved in some way. Not great, but well enough for an unpretentious game engine. It's not feasible without a lot of work and knowledge, but it's technically possible. Second I don't think <i>no progress</i> is the better way to phrase it. A lot was already done to reduce hallucination, and there are possible steps to reduce it in a given session, although it remains that there's no sign of it ever ceasing to be and I don't think it ever will. Third, and it's actually part of the first but deserves particular mention, simulating creativity is their whole point. It is far from perfect, but they can do an impressive work already, and again good enough for a casual game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-25T07:10:09-08:00","id":1556985,"title":"","content":"Update<br /> <br /> After 16 &quot;sessions&quot; (individual chats that cover roughly what a human to humans game would do in a session, collected in a project with log documents) Claude just started gibbering nonsense and cried uncle (Yes I am anthropomorphising a little). I think mostly for the reasons stated above. Thanks for your comments.<br /> <br /> I think beyond a little philosophizing about the nature of cognition my main takeaway from this experience is that I really do miss playing MtAw (as opposed to perennially STing). It would be fun to find a human group to play with.<br /> <br /> Merry Christmas!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T17:52:20-08:00","id":1557017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556897-using-ai-to-do-a-solo-chronicle?p=1556985#post1556985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Update<br /> <br /> After 16 &quot;sessions&quot; (individual chats that cover roughly what a human to humans game would do in a session, collected in a project with log documents) Claude just started gibbering nonsense and cried uncle (Yes I am anthropomorphising a little). I think mostly for the reasons stated above. Thanks for your comments.<br /> <br /> I think beyond a little philosophizing about the nature of cognition my main takeaway from this experience is that I really do miss playing MtAw (as opposed to perennially STing). It would be fun to find a human group to play with.<br /> <br /> Merry Christmas!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Session degradation due to excessive context<br /> <br /> To deal with this kind of situation you have to summarize key information to port to new fresh sessions without carrying the whole weight in tokens.<br /> <br /> It's feasible, I've been doing that a lot lately, but not a casual thing to do, it takes some study and a lot of work and patience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T18:04:03-08:00","id":1557018,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> So I was having it create session notes at the end of each session and then review these notes at the beginning of each session. What method would you use? I genuinely like the character I created and the two mysteries that Claude came up with (You are correct that inventiveness is not Claude's main problem) so it would be great to be able to continue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-28T03:41:12-08:00","id":1557054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556897-using-ai-to-do-a-solo-chronicle?p=1557018#post1557018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> So I was having it create session notes at the end of each session and then review these notes at the beginning of each session. What method would you use? I genuinely like the character I created and the two mysteries that Claude came up with (You are correct that inventiveness is not Claude's main problem) so it would be great to be able to continue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to understand better the specific API you're using, and I'm not yet sufficiently familiar with Claude's consumer apps, so I can't guide you a lot, but...<br /> <br /> First you have to find out precisely when Claude is carrying information from one chat session to the other. Every chat session with a LLM has a <i>context window</i>, which is basically the cache of data the model is juggling with at the moment. Any, absolutely <i>any</i> information in the session occupies the context window, through an information unit called <i>token</i>. Everything you say is tokens, everything Claude says is tokens, if you upload a file or Claude makes a search all those things are tokens.<br /> <br /> And critically, tokens aren't removed, only added. Once information enters a session it's there to stay.<br /> <br /> So, if a given session remember <i>anything at all</i> of previous sessions, then they're not actually new sessions. To be a new session it has to start with a clean memory. Any info being carried must be through other applications or you inserting notes, and that should be fairly easy to find out. Look for any setting or option that helps a session start from where the other stopped, and you'll have the culprit for inflating token count.<br /> <br /> Your solution is, in short: disable anything that carries info from one session to another, find out how to start a completely new, blank-slate session, and have every key information copied elsewhere, so you can copy-past it manually into the new session, guaranteeing it only has the context it needs and nothing else. You can use other sessions to explore how Claude works and how to optimize your notes, reducing the token count even more without loosing important stuff, but how exactly to optimize is something that varies a lot from model to model, I can't help with Claude yet (I may be in the near future, not sure yet).<br /> <br /> One important note here is that LLMs mimic human language, but don't process information like humans. Almost always that means we tend to over-explain and make unnecessarily detailed prompts that don't really add anything and actually confuses them. So it's always worth a shot to make some tests and trim down your notes, even beyond what you would consider reasonable intuitively. That's even more true if you have lots of notes that may actually contextualize each other, as the LLM kind of reads the whole Context Window at once (until it degrades).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T12:55:47-08:00","id":1557278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556897-using-ai-to-do-a-solo-chronicle?p=1557054#post1557054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your solution is, in short: disable anything that carries info from one session to another, find out how to start a completely new, blank-slate session, and have every key information copied elsewhere, so you can copy-past it manually into the new session, guaranteeing it only has the context it needs and nothing else. You can use other sessions to explore how Claude works and how to optimize your notes, reducing the token count even more without loosing important stuff, but how exactly to optimize is something that varies a lot from model to model, I can't help with Claude yet (I may be in the near future, not sure yet).</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume your initial prompt (how to be a story-teller, the rules of the games, or at least the name of the game you want to play since they tend to have consumed all of the text) should add to the summary.<br /> <br /> But in addition, you could have setting specific background info, NPCs (and their stats) political factions. All the stuff a GM would setup, but may be harder to do (and transfer, without player knowledge) or could be worked on in a session 0.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there are custom models where this could be automated (including things like aspirations)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T13:11:01-08:00","id":1557281,"title":"","content":"It does an ok job remembering the basic mechanics of the game. I've been running CoD one shots for the past week rather than trying to do a full Mage chronicle, and it can make it through a short investigation scenario before its context window runs out.<br /> <br /> it will actually suggest aspirations based on game play if you ask. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, being &quot;creative&quot; is not its problem, its being consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T03:27:59-08:00","id":1557339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556897-using-ai-to-do-a-solo-chronicle?p=1557278#post1557278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there are custom models where this could be automated (including things like aspirations)</div> </div> </div> </div>As the case is about continuing a game, initial prompt seems to be something already done, but yes, you can always study and iterate to learn the best way to bootstrap a Storyteller Session. Having a dedicated archive of prompts (which may be as simple as a TXT doc) is a must.<br /> <br /> But custom models, I don't think so. This is really hard and costly to do. It means running your own AI server, and while this is doable in a (very good) PC for other generative AI, LLMs are simply too far beyond what you can process with regular equipment. So we're talking a lot of work and resources to maintain a service that probably won't get much return.<br /> <br /> The problem with LLMs is the context window. A generative AI doing images, sounds or movies only have to look at a few data points at a time to decide what to do with a given area, then discard this information and look for the next set of data points to work another area, so it's never really processing anything resembling the whole piece at a time. LLMs have some tricks nowadays to not have to process each and every word, but the point <u><b>is</b></u> to remember the whole session, and that means it can't discard any data, only accumulate. Every new prompt in a session isn't just processing what you just said, but processing the whole session again to make a meaningful response. Add that to the sheer amount of data needed for training, and they're just not something we'll have in home computers for a very long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}